A||||12||artherd||LOVE my 17" wheels!!||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||07-13-2001||10:49 PM||||Just thought I'd post a quick message, that the Fiero is just *made* for 17" wheel/tyre setups :)<P>I have 17x7 wiht 40mm offset with Dunlop Sport W10 tyres front and rear (thanks Trav!)on the formula, and the car is great!<P>SO MUCH more stable on the freeway, and twice as nimble!  Pontiac should be brought up on charges for sticking an olympic runner of a chassis into wal-martt slippers (the 14-15" stock setups :)<P>Unlike many, I found the 17" setup not to have a noticable increase in road harshness or *any* detriment to ride quality.  Infact, I belive the ride is a bit smoother, more clean than it had been before!  The roads around here are generally "pretty" good however, so if you live in Pothole City(TM) things might be different.  In my case, both ride quality, AND handling improved dramatically!<P>I would say to anyone considering an 17" tyre setup to DO IT, DO IT!   Though I would recomend 17x8 in the rear.  Remenber to use a high performance tyre such as the dunlops, or Pirelli's P7000, or PZero.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
