Z||000009||ggriner||07-20-2001||04:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DecadenceR:<BR><B>Just be careful your roof doesn't crack... Because, as we all know in here, 17" rims ALWAYS makes your roof crack...<BR>LMAO    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Pardon my ignorance, but does the use of 17" wheels 'actually' cause any kind of body damage or is it just and inside joke?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||07-20-2001||04:53 PM||||No body damage what so ever , that was just some dumbass who posted that a while back. We have since run him off the list..he has returned under another name.<P>I have run 17's for a year now with a really stiff suspension , with no problems<P>Just picked up 2 ADR 17" wheels , for $100 , ins. co claim. My friend had a car wash incident , insurance is buying him 2 new wheels so I get the old scraped up ones.<P>Looking at Nitto drag radials , or some BFG drag radials to mount on them<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wannabe||07-20-2001||05:37 PM||||Questions, questions, questions. I'm shopping around for a set of rims that will fit my Formula properly without sticking out too far, but  it seems to be a tough go. The best deal I have found is a set of billet wheels 16x7 38mm offset front, and 16x8 42mm offset rear. The question is, the factory 15x7 35mm offset wheels stick out from the front fenders, 16x7 38mm won't be much better. Most aftermatket rims come in at 35-42mm offset, regardless of the width. Is there anything easy to find and reasonably priced with enough offset for the front, or do I just give up and go for the good deal????||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||07-20-2001||05:53 PM||||It's my understanding (and I'm not too experienced with wheels) that the greater the offset the more it "tucks" under the fender.  Meaning a 38mm offset won't stick out as far as the stock 35mm offset.<P>I have been told to get the highest possible offset (around 40mm at least) for the best results. <P>Again, I could be wrong (it wouldn't be the first time!).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||1
